---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About me page for Simon Xiang.">
  <header class="page-header about-header">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="about-copy">
      Hi, I'm Simon. I studied pure mathematics at UT Austin and graduated in
      Fall 2023. I was mainly interested in things like TQFTs and
      low-dimensional topology. At some point I realized I wanted to make a
      real-world impact instead of studying ∞-categories, so I pivoted to stuff
      like probability (measure theory) and quantum information science.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="about-interjection" aria-labelledby="sesame-title">
    <figure>
      <button
        class="sesame-photo"
        type="button"
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-controls="sesame-theorem"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/sesame.jpeg"
          alt="Sesame, a majestic tabby cat, lounging on his cat tree in the late-afternoon sun"
          width="2302"
          height="2351"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </button>
      <figcaption id="sesame-title">
        Interjection: a picture of my cat, Sesame.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="sesame-theorem" id="sesame-theorem" hidden>
      <em>Lemma.</em> Every sufficiently warm rectangle eventually contains a cat.
      <span aria-hidden="true">∎</span>
    </p>
  </div>
  <p class="about-copy">
    After graduating I worked as a quantitative researcher for a small family
    office called North Cut Trading, spun off from QuantLab. I worked here for
    about a year, before deciding that building things was more fun than reading
    papers. Now I work as a software engineer at AWS. If you want to chat about
    math, computers, or anything really - feel free to <a
      href="mailto:simonzx.xiang@proton.me">reach out!</a
    >
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const sesameButton =
    document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.sesame-photo');
  const theorem = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#sesame-theorem');

  sesameButton?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const reveal = theorem?.hidden ?? false;
    if (theorem) theorem.hidden = !reveal;
    sesameButton.ariaExpanded = String(reveal);
  });
</script>
